    dict(key='08-act-5', kind='console', title='Act Five — The bill',
         body='FIVE. The bill.\n  the secrets service holds every secret, so it needs its own access control, audit and backups\n  the application still needs a first credential to prove who it is\n  leases and rotation need applications that can reconnect with a new login without a restart\n  a scanner finds only what it has patterns for, so it is one check, not a guarantee',
         narration='Fifth demo: the bill. [[slnc 400]] The secrets service now holds every secret. [[slnc 300]] So it needs its own access control, audit trail, and backups. [[slnc 600]] The application still needs a first credential, to prove who it is. [[slnc 300]] Platform identity, in the advanced track, removes that last secret. [[slnc 600]] Applications must reconnect with new logins, without a restart. [[slnc 300]] And a scanner finds only what it has patterns for.'),
